# Agent Decision Records (AgDR)

This project uses [Agent Decision Records](https://www.me2resh.com/blog/agent-decision-records) (AgDR): lightweight, versioned records of **non-obvious technical decisions** so humans and future agents know *why* something was chosen.

## When you MUST write an AgDR (stop and document first)

Before merging or finishing work, add a new file under `docs/agdr/` if you:

- Change **training / evaluation semantics** (e.g. new metrics, defaults that alter Phase 1–5 meaning).
- Introduce or move **hardware calibration** (gains, offsets, noise profiles, CSV schema).
- Add dependencies, change **Python version bounds**, or alter **CLI contracts** (`hwa-*` entrypoints).
- Choose among **multiple real approaches** (not trivial renames or obvious bugfixes).

If you catch yourself saying “we’ll use X” or comparing “X vs Y” for anything in `src/hwa_cim/`, `pyproject.toml`, or thesis pipeline docs — **write the AgDR first**, then implement.

## Where and how

| Item | Convention |
|------|----------------|
| Location | `docs/agdr/AgDR-{NNNN}-{short-kebab-title}.md` |
| Next ID | One greater than the highest existing `AgDR-NNNN` in `docs/agdr/` |
| Template | Copy from [docs/agdr/TEMPLATE.md](docs/agdr/TEMPLATE.md) |
| Status | `proposed` until merged; then `executed` (or `superseded` with pointer to replacement) |

Fill **Context**, **Options Considered** (table), **Decision**, **Consequences**, and the **Y-statement** at the top. Keep the record honest about tradeoffs (e.g. schematic vs layout, ideal vs hardware-shaped metrics).

## Project scope hint

**sram-hwa-hybrid-ai** (`hwa-cim` on PyPI/pip) is a hardware-aware training pipeline for hybrid (analog + digital) SRAM AI acceleration—a C-2C compute-in-memory macro (MNIST micro-MLP, Phases 1–5). Decisions that affect comparability of thesis numbers or the hardware–software boundary belong in AgDR.

Do **not** edit the plan file in `.cursor/plans/` when documenting decisions — copy the substance into `docs/agdr/` if it was a real decision.
